Zero updater 0.11 independent source review

Reviewed read-only by the installer_lifecycle collaborator on 2026-11-17.
Files: main.zero.part, recovery.zero.part, sha256.zero.part, declarations,
README.txt, FORMAT.txt and focused recovery tests.

No blocking defect found in full-record chain validation, prefix/high-water
preservation, payload copy and independent rehash, exact source-journal
recheck, source-lock/evidence preservation or exclusive target semantics.
Worker flushes and closes owned handles. Recovery does not drop whole invalid
records or infer that a source lock is stale; it writes a new snapshot only.

Review clarification applied to README: metadata is always validated, but a
release counter <= high-water mark is a no-op and its unused inbox image is
not hashed. A corrupted NEWER image fails verification.

Limits remain explicit: final source recheck is a point-in-time snapshot,
not a lock against subsequent adversarial mutations. Parent directories are
not fsynced; power-loss ordering/durability of rename is not guaranteed.
This review does not claim hardware power-loss simulation, native Windows,
network transport, publisher authentication, scheduler or boot activation.

Focused testing separately caught error-code masking after a failed recovery
copy. Hash comparison now runs only after successful worker I/O, preserving
the actual write/flush failure code 74. The regression is exercised through
RLIMIT_FSIZE and injected fsync errors in test-recovery.py.
